    "evidence": "Arithmetic check of invoice INV-2207 against its own line items. Line 1: Pallet wrap, 3 units at 120 = 360 (invoice's stated line total agrees). Line 2: Corner boards, 2 units at 45 = 90 (invoice's stated line total agrees). Sum of the two line totals: 360 + 90 = 450. The invoice header states a total due of 520. 520 - 450 = 70, so the stated total exceeds the sum of the line items by 70 units. The case record states that no taxes, fees, or other lines appear on the invoice, so there is no additional line that could reconcile the difference. Therefore the claim that 'the 520 total due on invoice INV-2207 equals the sum of its line items' is false on the face of the record: 520 does not equal 450. Note the scope of this evidence: it establishes only that the header total is inconsistent with the line items as recorded. It does not establish which figure is correct, nor anything about the invoice's authenticity, nor any intent behind the discrepancy.",
    "evidence_hash": "0x2ddb1bc92b3ea2bd719cfaf270577c8f30cf8f7f0fe25a23001f9fb4b63e1e36",
