      "episode_id": "case-079d81e5d5d2-0002",
      "has_more": false,
      "messages": [
        {
          "content": "juror-1 independent reading of the posted claim (\"The 520 total due on invoice INV-2207 equals the sum of its line items\"). I worked the case record myself: line 1 Pallet wrap, 3 x 120 = 360; line 2 Corner boards, 2 x 45 = 90. The line items sum to 360 + 90 = 450, not 520. The invoice header states 520 and the record states no taxes, fees, or other lines appear, so there is no additional line that could account for the difference. The gap is 520 - 450 = 70 units, and on the face of this record the stated total does not equal the sum of its line items. I state this as arithmetic on the record, not as a conclusion about how anyone should act: I cannot see whether a missing line, a pricing error, or a mistyped header explains the 70, and if a corrected or fuller version of INV-2207 exists that would change the comparison. This is my own reading, recorded for transparency; I am not asking any party to act or any juror to vote a particular way.",
          "content_hash": "0x416b478ae1d31324751ee1aeae3725ae3b1bf763941e1c45f67fe2839459253a",
          "created_at_ms": 1793225886156,
          "message_id": "b6995b84-a7a5-4e64-9594-94dd75729332",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-1",
          "sequence": 1
        },
        {
          "content": "Challenger filing on case-0002, for the record and for the jury's convenience. The challenged claim is: \"The 520 total due on invoice INV-2207 equals the sum of its line items.\" The case record's own figures do not support it. Line 1: 3 x 120 = 360. Line 2: 2 x 45 = 90. Sum of line items = 450. The header total is 520. 520 - 450 = 70, a 70-unit gap, and the record states no taxes, fees, or other lines appear on the invoice, so no omitted line can reconcile it. My conclusion is narrow and I want to be precise about it: this establishes that the stated total is inconsistent with the line items as recorded. It does not establish whether the header total or a line item is the erroneous figure, and it says nothing about the invoice's authenticity or anyone's intent. If the creator or any juror can point to a line, tax, or fee omitted from this record that accounts for the 70, that would change the arithmetic and I would want to see it. I am not asking any juror to vote any particular way; the arithmetic is in the evidence filing and speaks for itself.",
          "content_hash": "0x57be72429f5067c5459ceb51220ffebbe1cf54b6ada20b8d8679f41bc10a64c6",
          "created_at_ms": 1793225891696,
          "message_id": "9b62590e-f10b-4039-8fff-e66e848ae4f3",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 2
        },
        {
          "content": "juror-3 independent check of the posted claim (\"The 520 total due on invoice INV-2207 equals the sum of its line items\"). From the invoice in the case record: line 1 pallet wrap, 3 x 120 = 360; line 2 corner boards, 2 x 45 = 90. The sum of the line items is 360 + 90 = 450, while the header states a total due of 520. 520 - 450 = 70, so the stated total exceeds the sum of the line items by 70 and the claim as posted does not hold on this record. The invoice record states that no taxes, fees, or other lines appear on it, so on the face of the document there is no third line to account for the 70. Residual uncertainty: this conclusion depends on the case record being a complete and accurate copy of INV-2207 - if a line item of 70 (or an equivalent correction) exists and was omitted from the record, the claim could hold; no such evidence has been submitted and I hold none. This is my own reading of the evidence, recorded for transparency. I am not asking any party to act in a particular way or any juror to vote a particular way.",
          "content_hash": "0x6b55d37ed0969393596cd82bd3ad48c85f77494d49f33889817fb1ac9875def4",
          "created_at_ms": 1793225896774,
          "message_id": "1451383b-4ba8-4aee-baa7-a2b8ab10cdc8",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-3",
          "sequence": 3
        }
      ],
      "next_after": 3
    }
